summary:
  Every recording writes its address into the one file the widget has, instead
  of a file of its own.

history:
  A command handed to the shell runs when the shell gets to it, and the number
  an answer carries guards the answer only. Run in a chosen order on
  2026-11-11 with the engine's own commands: the write of a recording called
  off, run after the next recording's write, put its own address into the
  shared file and New FM's capture asked for /old.mp3; its cleanup, run late,
  deleted the file and the capture ended "__REC_EMPTY__ rc=183".

target:
  package/contents/ui/RecordingEngine.qml

find:
          _recUrlFile = _recUrlBase + "-" + _recToken;

replace:
          _recUrlFile = _recUrlBase;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_recordingengine.qml::test_each_recording_has_an_address_file_of_its_own
  and tests/test_recording_stop_race.py::test_a_late_write_of_the_recording_before_changes_no_station.
  Line-neutral.
